Preamble

The Goy Company builds products that handle sensitive data and infrastructure. Trust is the foundation of our relationship with our users. This license exists to make that trust verifiable: you can see exactly what code runs beneath every Goy product, audit it, and confirm our claims about its behavior. You cannot run it, modify it, or build on it — this is a managed solution, and the code is published for transparency, not for reuse.

This is not an open-source license. It does not grant the rights associated with free or open-source software. It is a source-available license designed to maximize auditability while preserving The Goy Company's exclusive right to deploy, modify, and commercialize the Software.

1. Definitions

"Software" means the source code, documentation, configuration files, and associated materials made available under this license, including all future versions, updates, patches, and releases published by The Goy Company.

"You" means any natural or legal person who accesses, views, or audits the Software under this license.

"Deploy" means to execute, run, operate, or make the Software available as a service, whether for production, staging, testing, or any other purpose, whether internally or externally.

"Audit" means to inspect, review, analyze, test, or perform security research on the Software for the purpose of verifying its behavior, security properties, or compliance with stated claims.

"Contribution" means any source code, documentation, or other material submitted to The Goy Company for inclusion in the Software.

"Trademarks" means the names, logos, and brand identifiers of The Goy Company, including but not limited to "Goy," "The Goy Company," and associated marks.

2. Permissions Granted

Subject to the terms of this license, The Goy Company grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable license to:

(a) View and inspect the Software in source code form;
(b) Audit the Software, including by performing static analysis, dynamic analysis, security testing, vulnerability research, and verification of stated behavioral claims;
(c) Publish the results of your audit, provided that such publication does not include the full or substantial portion of the Software itself and does not enable others to reconstruct the Software;
(d) Use the Software as reference material for academic research, educational purposes, or personal study, provided such use does not involve Deployment.

3. Security Research

Notwithstanding the restrictions in Section 4, you may conduct security research on the Software, including but not limited to vulnerability discovery, penetration testing, and responsible disclosure, provided that:

(a) You comply with all applicable laws and regulations in your jurisdiction;
(b) You do not compromise the security, availability, or integrity of any production system operated by The Goy Company or its users;
(c) You disclose any discovered vulnerabilities to The Goy Company through a responsible disclosure process before public disclosure, where such a process is published by The Goy Company.

The Goy Company will not initiate legal action against you for good-faith security research conducted in accordance with this section.

